flowchart LR
accTitle: Perception and grounding have different effects
accDescr: Perception reads a snapshot and returns a provenance-bearing observation with the source version. Grounding submits a typed state-changing request through the dispatch and world adapter boundary. This chapter does not repeat the detailed gates from Chapter 19.

    SNAP[Versioned simulated snapshot]
    SNAP --> READ[Perception action<br/>read only]
    READ --> OBS[Observation<br/>value, evidence, provenance,<br/>source version]
    CAND[Proposed candidate] --> WRITE[Grounding request<br/>domain write]
    WRITE --> DISPATCH[Dispatcher and world adapter<br/>Chapter 19]
    DISPATCH --> NEXT[New current snapshot]
